paths: list[tuple[str, int]]` five most frequent paths, count descending then path ascending\n2026-10-01T12:00:00Z GET /api/users 200 12.5 843\n2026-10-01T12:00:01Z POST /api/users 201 40 120\n2026-10-01T12:00:02Z GET /api/users/7 404 3.1\ngarbage line here\n2026-10-01T12:00:03Z GET /api/users 500 120.0 0\n2026-10-01T12:00:04Z GET /health 200 0.4\n\"\"\"Implement parse_line and summarize here. See FORMAT.md.\"\"\"\n\u001b[31m[bat error]\u001b[0m: 'tests/*.py': No such file or directory (os error 2)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CRhdaUYbbWutQkMeeyb7nH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
